  "heading": "\\integer.equivalence",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{integer equivalence relation}\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{\\sim_{\\mathbb{Z}}}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\integer.equivalence]\nDefines: R is \\equivalence.relation:on{\\naturals.set \\.set.cross./ \\naturals.set}\nexpresses:\n. let: (n1, m1), (n2, m2) \"in\" (.\\naturals.set \\.set.cross./ \\naturals.set.)\n  then:\n  . have: R( (n1, m1), (n2, m2) )\n    iff: n1 + m2 = n2 + m1\nDocumented:\n. called: \"integer equivalence relation\"\n. written: \"\\sim_{\\mathbb{Z}}\"\n. description: \"The relation on pairs of naturals that identifies $(n_1, m_1)$\n                with $(n_2, m_2)$ exactly when $n_1 + m_2 = n_2 + m_1$. This is\n                the cross-multiplied form of $n_1 - m_1 = n_2 - m_2$, expressed\n                with addition alone, and it is an equivalence relation.\"\nId: \"ee34451f-a1b6-4339-9ec4-f260c0a4d395\"",
